# HopOn Netherlands

HopOn is a mobile-first guide to real places in Amsterdam, Rotterdam and Utrecht. Search and filter the curated catalog, explore places on a MapLibre map, view nearby mobility hubs and build a tab-only Discover draft.

## Run locally (Windows PowerShell)

Terminal 1, from the repository root:

```powershell
.\.tools\run-backend.ps1
```

This starts the Java 27 / Spring Boot API at `http://localhost:8080` using the Gradle 9.8.2 wrapper.

Terminal 2, from the repository root:

```powershell
cd frontend
npm ci
npm start
```

Use a Node.js version matching `^22.22.3 || ^24.15.0 || ^26.0.0` from `frontend/package.json`. Open `http://localhost:4200`. Angular proxies `/api/**` to the backend. `npm run start:lan` serves the UI on the local network.

## Checks

From `frontend/`, run `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm test` and `npm run build`.

For browser E2E, keep the backend running, install Chromium once with `npx playwright install chromium`, then run `npm run test:e2e`. The tests start a separate Angular server on port 4300 and use the real API proxy.

The backend uses in-memory H2, so its data resets when it stops. The city catalog is a static OpenStreetMap snapshot; map styles and tiles require a network connection.
